'''Murley''' was a [[Loth-cat]] owned by the [[Mandalorian]] [[Sabine Wren]] during the [[New Republic Era|time]] of the [[New Republic]], living alongside Wren in the [[LothalNet comm tower E-272]] on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]]. Around [[9 ABY]], the [[cat]] spent [[time]] around Wren during her attempts to unlock a [[Arcana Star Map|compass]] containing a [[star map]] and briefly encountered Wren's former Master, [[Ahsoka Tano]]. Wren later departed on a [[Quest to find Ezra Bridger|quest]] to find [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ezra Bridger]], leaving Murley on Lothal.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Uh-uh. Looking for a key, okay?|Sabine Wren to Murley, working to decipher the star map|<ref name="Part One" />}}
[[File:SabinesLothCat-MaA.jpg|thumb|right|280px|Wren scratches Murley.]]
The [[Loth-cat]] Murley<ref name="Databank" /> was owned by<ref name="SWE" /> the [[Mandalorian]] [[artist]] [[Sabine Wren]].<ref name="Part One" /> Wren named the tooka<ref name="SWE" /> and lived with him on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]] in [[LothalNet comm tower E-272]] during the [[New Republic Era]],<ref name="Part One" /> around [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Date">{{AhsokaSeriesDate}}</ref> When Wren returned to the [[Comm tower|tower]] after refusing to attend a [[Spectres mural ceremony|ceremony]], Murley woke from a [[Sleep|nap]] and greeted<ref name="Part One" /> his<ref name="Dagobah" /> companion, who scratched his chin. Wren then retrieved a container of<ref name="Part One" /> special [[Foodstuff|pellets]],<ref name="Databank" /> poured the food into a bowl, and set it down on a crate for Murley. Wren petted the [[cat]] as he [[Diet|ate]] before locating a [[hologram]] of her friend<ref name="Part One" /> and fellow [[Spectres|rebel]], the [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]]<ref name="SWE" /> [[Ezra Bridger]].<ref name="Part One" />

The cat was resting on a table when Wren brought back a [[Arcana Star Map|compass]] containing a [[star map]] taken from her former Master, [[Ahsoka Tano]]. Murley took an interest in the [[compass]], sniffing it before hissing and pawing at the item<ref name="Part One" /> like a toy.<ref name="SWE" /> Wren chastised the creature and proceeded to project a hologram of [[Nightsisters' Temple|ruins]] on the world [[Arcana]] over where Murley stood, causing the animal to jump to the floor and leave promptly. The Mandalorian later exited the living space to the tower's catwalk, where Murley joined her, meowing and peering upward. Wren took notice and bent down, petting Murley and talking to him about an upcoming trip. The cat sniffed her before noticing and screeching at the presence of a [[HK-87 assassin droid]].<ref name="Part One" />

[[File:MurleyAhsoka.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Murley receives a visit from Ahsoka Tano.]]
Murley later interacted with Tano, who crouched in front of the Loth-cat when visiting the tower. Murley hung back when Tano entered the tower's interior but kept her within sight and wailed at the appearance of a second [[assassin droid]], who ambushed Tano. Tano destroyed the [[droid]], and Murley hissed at its decapitated head. The Loth-cat subsequently snoozed but raised his head upon Wren's return. The Mandalorian then petted him. Wren later left Lothal&mdash;and Murley&mdash;on a [[Quest to find Ezra Bridger|quest]] in search of Bridger,<ref name="Part Two">{{Ahsoka|Part Two: Toil and Trouble}}</ref> just as she told her pet she would do.<ref name="Part One" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|I think I'm going on a trip.''"<br />[Murley purrs, then screeches]|quoteend=0|Murley's reaction to Sabine Wren and an assassin droid|<ref name="Part One" />}}
Murley was a Loth-cat,<ref name="Part One" /> a breed of [[tooka]].<ref name="Helmet Collection 36">{{HelmetCollectionCite|36|Databank A-Z}}</ref> His fur, soft to the touch,<ref name="Poster">{{ThisWeek|p02W3Y3xilw|Dispatch: Loth-cat Character Poster|sw_url=video/loth-cat-character-poster-this-week-in-star-wars-dispatch}}</ref> was [[Color|tan]] and white, interspersed with patterns of brown spots and stripes. Murley possessed black [[eye]]s, black skin, and pointy ears,<ref name="Part One" /> as well as sharp [[Tooth|teeth]] and [[claw]]s.<ref name="Databank" /> The tooka cat was one [[foot]], nine inches tall (fifty-four [[centimeter]]s); two feet, four inches long (seventy centimeters); and weighed ten [[kilogram]]s (twenty-two [[pound]]s).<ref name="LifeSize" />

[[File:MurleyDatabank.jpg|thumb|right|275px|Murley]]
Although not domesticated, Murley enjoyed<ref name="Databank" /> spending time with Sabine Wren, greeting and following her around<ref name="Part One" /> in her tower, finding the living space comfortable.<ref name="Databank" /> The cat liked being pet and scratched beneath the chin, purring when Wren did so. Murley enjoyed feeding time, sniffing and staring intently at Wren while she prepared his food and licking his lips upon receiving it.<ref name="Part One" /> Murley also took frequent naps<ref name="Part One" /><ref name="Part Two" /> among Wren's belongings<ref name="Databank" /> and sometimes exhibited a silently judging stare.<ref name="Poster" />

The Loth-cat treated the star compass Wren retrieved with distrust, growling and batting at it. The cat ran away when Wren activated a hologram that projected into Murley's space.<ref name="Part One" /> The loyal<ref name="SWE" /> tooka<ref name="Helmet Collection 36" /> also showed disdain for HK-87 assassin droids, hissing at them when they attacked Wren<ref name="Part One" /> and Tano.<ref name="Part Two" />

==Skills and abilities==
Murley was adept at [[hunting]],<ref name="Databank" /> able to provide for himself outdoors.<ref name="SWE" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|My little Loth-cat, it was so cute. They sprung that cat on me one day. I just walked to set and it was a rehearsal for the scene and it was the first time I saw the cat come to life. It's got hilarious little turkey legs, which is my favorite part.''" [Laughs]|quoteend=0|Natasha Liu Bordizzo|<ref name="Commentary">{{SW|url=part-one-master-and-apprentice-commentary-gallery-ahsoka|text="Part One: Master and Apprentice" Commentary Gallery &#124; Ahsoka}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref>}}
[[File:Murley-Alzmann.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Concept art of Murley by Christian Alzmann]]
Murley was first pictured in a teaser for the [[Disney+]] live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]'', which was released on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|HnzNZ0Mdx4I|Ahsoka &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/ahsoka-teaser-trailer}}</ref> The Loth-cat's prop&mdash;designed by Legacy Effects&mdash;was displayed at the [[Lucasfilm]] Pavillion at [[Wikipedia:San Diego Comic-Con|San Diego Comic-Con]],<ref name="SDCC">{{SW|url=news/sdcc-2023-ahsoka-props|text=SDCC 2023: See ''Ahsoka'' Props and Costumes from the Lucasfilm Pavilion}}</ref> which was held from [[July 20]] to [[July 23]] the same year.<ref name="SDCC Date">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/comic-con-schedule-panels-san-diego-1235662842|text=Comic-Con 2023 Schedule: 'Star Trek,' 'The Walking Dead,' 'Harley Quinn' Headline Quieter Event Amid SAG-AFTRA Strike|author=[https://variety.com/author/adam-b-vary/ Adam B. Vary]|date=2023-07-14|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20230731225900}}</ref> Murley later debuted in "[[Part One: Master and Apprentice]]" and "[[Part Two: Toil and Trouble]],"&mdash;the first and second episodes of the series<ref name="Part One" /><ref name="Part Two" />&mdash;which simultaneously premiered on [[August 22]], 2023.<ref name="New Release Date">{{SW|url=news/ahsoka-new-premiere-date|text=''Ahsoka'' Premiere Moves Up to Tuesday, August 22|date=2023-08-18|quote=The two-episode premiere of ''Ahsoka'' will now arrive on Tuesday, August 22 at 6 p.m. PT on Disney+}}</ref> Murley was later named by the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] account on [[October 3]] that year,<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1709195376635318591|[[Star Wars]]|quote=Who's watching #Sabine's Loth-cat? We all are&hellip; on TikTok LIVE! Join the countdown to the #Ahsoka season finale with Lothal's cutest companion, Murley|archivedate=20231003133138}}</ref> promoting a video of the ''[[Star Wars Lofi]]'' series that features the cat.<ref name="Lofi">{{SWYouTube|uSqsyC780OY|Sabine's Loth-Cat &#124; Star Wars Lofi &#124; #Ahsoka}}</ref>

[[Christian Alzmann]]'s concept artwork of Murley in [[March]] [[2022]] shows the Loth-cat with light-green eyes and white fur with gray patterning. The color scheme in the illustration is an alternate depiction<ref name="Concept Art">{{SW|url=concept-art-ahsoka|text=Concept Art &#124; Ahsoka}} {{C|Slide 12}}</ref> to the black eyes and tan and white fur later used in ''Ahsoka''.<ref name="Part One" /> Sabine Wren's actor, [[Natasha Liu Bordizzo]], noted the cat's appearance during on-set rehearsal as a cute surprise, particularly enjoying his "hilarious little turkey legs."<ref name="Commentary" /> Murley's scenes were filmed on the proprietary [[Industrial Light & Magic]] [[Wikipedia:StageCraft|StageCraft]] technology on a soundstage known as "The Volume." Production teams relied on a combination of practical puppets and digital versions inserted after filming to bring the loth-cat to life.<ref name="ILM">{{ILM|url=stagecraft-premiere-d23|text=StageCraft Volume Makes Public Premiere at D23}}</ref>

In [[November]] 2023, ''Ahsoka'' series creator [[Dave Filoni]] appeared on [[Entertainment Weekly Books|''Entertainment Weekly'']]{{'s}} ''Star Wars'' podcast, [https://web.archive.org/web/20231219183047/https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/dagobah-dispatch-an-ew-star-wars-podcast/id1487489835 ''Dagobah Dispatch'']. Amazed by fans' concern for Murley's safety, Filoni spoke about the cat's ability to leave Wren's tower and independence as a wild animal, raising the possibility of a Murley-centric documentary. During the interview, Filoni referred to Murley using he/him pronouns,<ref name="Dagobah" /> a departure from the it/its pronouns presented in the series' audio description available on Disney+.<ref name="Audio" />

